**`ChatEntry.vue`** — Two additions:

1. **`cancellationTokenId` computed** — Returns `meta_data.cancellation_token_id` only when the message is not yet done (`!displayMessage.done`), so the button auto-hides once the message completes.

2. **Stop button** in the actions toolbar — Renders only when `cancellationTokenId` is truthy, calls `cancelMessage()` which delegates to `this.$storex.api.chats.cancelMessage(tokenId)`.

Looking at the comments, I need to update the `cancelMessage` API method to use `POST /api/chat/cancel` with a JSON body containing `token_id` instead of a GET request with a query parameter.

